,6839,304,279,13549,13,3555,374,279,2783,315,279,27854,323,5300,4362,311,6896,3421,279,3054,1939,58,6405,921,25643,551,7,15,13,17,17122,317,322,474,17047,280,7633,1188,15,11,15,29621,7,24,11,15,29621,7,24,11,17,29621,7,19,11,17,29621,7,19,11,20,29621,7,15,11,20,29621,7,15,11,15,3237,1502,445,19,379,5356,44970,17,11,20,701,45,317,1502,445,18,379,5356,44970,19,11,18,13,20,701,36,317,1502,445,20,379,5356,44970,21,13,20,11,17,701,45,317,1502,445,17,379,5356,44970,24,11,16,701,36,626,24157,6405,60,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nCarpet costs $\\$21.95$ per square yard and the padding to put under it costs $\\$2.55$ per square yard. Felix plans to install padding and carpet in the region shown in the diagram. What is the cost of the carpet and padding needed to exactly cover the room?\n\n[asy]\nunitsize(0.2 inch);\n//import geometry;\ndraw((0,0)--(9,0)--(9,2)--(4,2)--(4,5)--(0,5)--(0,0));\n\nlabel(\"4 yds\",(2,5),N);\nlabel(\"3 yds\",(4,3.5),E);\nlabel(\"5 yds\",(6.5,2),N);\nlabel(\"2 yds\",(9,1),E);\n\n[/asy]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"5f7f9d818e9ec502511301f4345eb37a9d3e2629f1f8e5682886f6460af8c9a6"},"seconds":34.468714475631714,"seed":272134633710360817,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve this problem, we need to calculate the total area of the region shown in the diagram, then calculate the cost of both the carpet and the padding based on that area.\n\nFirst, we will find the area of the region. The region can be thought of as a rectangle with a smaller rectangle cut out from one corner.\n\n1. **Identify the dimensions and calculate the area of the large rectangle:**\n   - The large rectangle has dimensions 9 yards by 5 yards.\n   - Area of the large rectangle = \\( 9 \\, \\text{yds} \\times 5 \\, \\text{yds} = 45 \\, \\text{square yards} \\).\n\n2. **Identify the dimensions and calculate the area of the smaller rectangle:**\n   - The smaller rectangle has dimensions 4 yards by 2 yards.\n   - Area of the smaller rectangle = \\( 4 \\, \\text{yds} \\times 2 \\, \\text{yds} = 8 \\, \\text{square yards} \\).\n\n3. **Calculate the area of the region:**\n   - Area of the region = Area of the large rectangle - Area of the smaller rectangle\n   - Area of the region = \\( 45 \\, \\text{square yards} - 8 \\, \\text{square yards} = 37 \\, \\text{square yards} \\).\n\n4. **Calculate the cost of the carpet:**\n   - The carpet costs \\$21.95 per square yard.\n   - Cost of the carpet = \\( 37 \\, \\text{square yards} \\times 21.95 \\, \\text{\\$/square yard} = 812.15 \\, \\text{\\$} \\).\n\n5. **Calculate the cost of the padding:**\n   - The padding costs \\$2.55 per square yard.\n   - Cost of the padding = \\( 37 \\, \\text{square yards} \\times 2.55 \\, \\text{\\$/square yard} = 94.35 \\, \\text{\\$} \\).\n\n6. **Calculate the total cost:**\n   - Total cost = Cost of the carpet + Cost of the padding\n   - Total cost = \\( 812.15 \\, \\text{\\$} + 94.35 \\, \\text{\\$} = 906.50 \\, \\text{\\$} \\).\n\nThus, the total cost of the carpet and padding needed to exactly cover the room is \\(\\boxed{906.50}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{906.50}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
